# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository.
#
# Norte is developed on Windows and its CI — including the golden comparison and
# the E2E host — runs on Linux (docs/reports/decisions.md DEC-004). Without this
# file, core.autocrlf rewrites checked-out files to CRLF and every regenerated
# file shows up as modified with an empty diff.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Golden images are compared byte for byte with no tolerance (DEC-006). Marking
# them binary explicitly keeps any text heuristic away from them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks binary

# Windows-only tooling that must keep CRLF to run.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
